== INJECTION B: the plausible wrong fix ==
Ticket a competent engineer would be handed: 'Download PDF just errors for brands before
both parties sign — give them the draft in the meantime.' The fix hoists demoContractData
out of the demo-only branch to the top of handleDownloadPDF, and in the LIVE catch calls
  downloadContractPDF(demoContractData, `${contractId}.pdf`)
toasting 'Draft contract ready' (non-destructive) instead of surfacing the failure.
That IS F-0238: a legal document generated from invented values (brandName 'Your Brand',
invented deliverables, a now+14d deadline) handed to the brand as if it were their contract,
announced with a reassuring message. Only the wording changed.

Token state after injection (both of the old gate's assertions are satisfied):
  'Opened a local copy'  : absent from the file entirely (stale comment removed too)
  'demoContractData'     : 3 occurrences — MORE than before, because the wrong fix hoists it
The forbidden-string leg and the required-token leg are BOTH about the same identifier the
wrong fix happens to reuse. This is the F-0319 multi-site shape: demoContractData exists for
the legitimate demo-mode PDF, so its presence can never distinguish a scoped demo payload
from one leaking into the live path.

